{"text": "Copying is pedestrian. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Copying is peculiar. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> On the one hand, copying makes us what we are. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Our bodies take shape from the transcription of protein templates, our languages from the mimicry of privileged sounds, our crafts from the repetition of prototypes. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Cultures hold together in the faithful transmission of rituals and rules of conduct. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To copy cell for cell, word for word, image for image, is to make the known world our own. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> On the other hand, we are not identical, nor do we wish to think of ourselves as clones. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Copying is ultimately imperfect, our errors eventually our heirs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The more widespread the act of copying, the greater the likelihood of significant mistranscription. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Genetic slip or evolution, written mistake or midrash, miscopying raises hard questions about identity, security, and integrity. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The same technical advances that make our skill at copying so impressive also intensify the dilemmas of forgery. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> We use copies to certify originals, originals to certify copies, then we stand confused.", "alignment": {"characters": ["C", "o", "p", "y", "i", "n", "g", " ", "i", "s", " ", "p", "e", "d", "e", "s", "t", "r", "i", "a", "n", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "C", "o", "p", "y", "i", "n", "g", " ", "i", "s", " ", "p", "e", "c", "u", "l", "i", "a", "r", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "O", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "o", "n", "e", " ", "h", "a", "n", "d", ",", " ", "c", "o", "p", "y", "i", "n", "g", " ", "m", "a", "k", "e", "s", " ", "u", "s", " ", "w", "h", "a", "t", " ", "w", "e", " ", "a", "r", "e", ".", " 